-- A seam-shaped (top-level IMPLIES) export whose goal variable is
-- deliberately never emitted (R4) is referenced by another decision — but
-- only THROUGH an inlined parameterized function. The dangling-reference
-- guard must see references that travel through inlined bodies, or the
-- emitter exits 0 and the interview dies at runtime with
-- DAErrorMissingVariable on `seam_rule` (the direct-reference control is
-- already refused; this fixture pins the inlined path).

§ `Seam ref via fn`
    GIVEN `scope flag` IS A BOOLEAN
          `req flag` IS A BOOLEAN

@export the main gate
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `main gate` amount IF `wrap` amount

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wrap` x IS x GREATER THAN 0 AND `seam rule`

@export the seam rule
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `seam rule` IF `scope flag` IMPLIES `req flag`
